 "title": "Counting war",
 "hook": "Researchers in Uppsala log every deadly clash they can verify. Here is what their records show for Ukraine, Syria and Sudan.",
 "notes": "Uppsala Conflict Data Program (UCDP): Georeferenced Event Dataset 26.1 (to December 2025) extended with preliminary Candidate events to August 2026. An event is an incident of organised violence with at least one death; events are grouped by month into cells of about 25 km, and circle size grows with the number of events. UCDP counts only deaths it can confirm from reports, so its figures are conservative; other estimates, especially of military deaths, are much higher. Events that could not be located below country level are not shown. Candidate data for 2026 is less complete. Events in Russia (for example Kursk) are not included in the Ukraine map.",
